I closed #1063 and left a comment on it. I skipped every other issue on the list because this session did no work on them.

• #1063 (closed): commit 318ea3e0 fixes /bg, which was the last open part. /bg now waits on sh first, then gives its output readers 2 seconds. If a background process it started still holds the output after that, a note goes into the job's output saying so. Anything that process writes later is still added below the note. Before the fix, the new test failed on the old code. After it, all 7 /bg tests pass, and the positive control (stretching the grace to 600s) turned the two new tests red until I restored it. The /watch part was already fixed on Day 237 (00d1dfc6). While working on this I found that /bg kill reports the job killed while the shell keeps running; that's filed as #1077 and not fixed here.
